<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The app's privacy manifest (native/AGENTS.md → "App Store": what we tell
  Apple and why; checked by native/tools/store-check.py).

  No tracking, no analytics, no advertising, and no code that collects data
  for the developer. The app talks to the workspaces its user adds — servers
  they run — and, for its remote kill switch, fetches
  https://xbin.dev/app/ios.json (no identifiers sent). Neither is data the
  developer collects.

  App tunnels (D204, native/spec/tunnel.md): the app links IrohLib (n0's
  iroh-ffi, open source) to reach a workspace that turned tunnels on. It
  connects only out, to that workspace, through the relay the workspace
  names: n0's public relays or one the workspace's operator runs. The relay
  sees the device's IP address and connection metadata, never content (Noise
  inside QUIC). That is the user's own connection to their own server, not
  data the developer collects, so nothing is declared below for it
  (website/privacy.html says who sees what).

  Push is the exception once it ships: the app then registers its APNs
  device token with the push relay run by the xbin project (native/spec/
  push.md). While XbinPushRelay in Support/App-Info.plist is empty, push is
  off and nothing reaches a relay, so nothing is declared below. When it
  names the project's relay, declare NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeDeviceID
  (not linked, not tracking, App Functionality) here and in App Store
  Connect's App Privacy — store-check.py fails until both agree.
--><plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<!-- The app's own settings, caches and scene state (AppSettings,
		     TerminalPrefs, RemoteConfig, LiveActivities, @SceneStorage). -->
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<!-- SwiftTerm's kitty graphics protocol stat()s and fstat()s image
		     files in the app's temporary directory and shared memory to
		     check their type and size (KittyGraphics.swift). -->
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<!-- IrohLib (app tunnels): its categories come from `nm -u` on a
		     build that links it (plans/app-tunnel.md Phase 6) — expected
		     SystemBootTime 35F9.1 if _mach_absolute_time appears, DiskSpace
		     only if statfs-type symbols do. Pending that report; once it is
		     in, list them here AND in store-check.py's IROHLIB_APIS, which
		     fails while project.yml links IrohLib without them. -->
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
